{
  "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
  "total_duration_s": 69.7,
  "total_frames_30fps": 2091,
  "segments": [
    {
      "seg_id": "N01",
      "text": "A kilometer down on the pitch-black ocean floor, deep-sea cameras cross a literal shoreline\u2014into an underwater lake.",
      "rate": "+3%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 0.1,
      "end": 6.396,
      "duration": 6.296,
      "pause_after": 0.22,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "Waves ripple across its mirror-like surface, while dark streams pour down the seabed slope.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 6.616,
      "end": 11.572,
      "duration": 4.956,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "Its secret is buried ancient salt. Dissolving beneath the Gulf of Mexico and the Red Sea, it creates brine up to eight times saltier than seawater.",
      "rate": "+0%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 11.832,
      "end": 20.628,
      "duration": 8.795,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N04",
      "text": "Too heavy to mix, that dense brine pools in seafloor basins\u2014trapping toxic methane and sulfur with zero oxygen.",
      "rate": "+0%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 20.888,
      "end": 27.73,
      "duration": 6.842,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N05",
      "text": "Any crab or fish that strays across the rim suffers instant anoxic shock. Yet dense beds of mussels and tubeworms thrive right along that deadly edge.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "+1Hz",
      "start": 28.01,
      "end": 36.575,
      "duration": 8.565,
      "pause_after": 0.25,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N06",
      "text": "In 2022, scientists dove 1,770 meters into the Red Sea\u2014and pulled mud cores from untouched brine pools. Without burrowing animals, those layers preserve a thousand years of earthquakes and tsunamis.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 36.825,
      "end": 50.942,
      "duration": 14.117,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N07",
      "text": "Researchers also test these chemical boundaries as stand-ins for icy moons like Europa. Of course, that doesn't prove life exists beyond Earth.",
      "rate": "-2%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 51.202,
      "end": 60.292,
      "duration": 9.091,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N08",
      "text": "Deep-sea brine pools aren't alien portals. They're toxic underwater lakes\u2014recording Earth's violent past and fueling life in total darkness.",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 60.572,
      "end": 69.442,
      "duration": 8.87,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    }
  ],
